From ba36ed5c00bb50ec327ec29091916998d4617125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bodapatisaikrishna <saikrishnabodapati@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:23:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] kernel-open: guard nv_audio_dynamic_power against non-HDA
 drivers

nv_audio_dynamic_power() calls pci_get_drvdata() on the GPU audio
function and casts the result to struct snd_card * without checking
the bound driver. When a non-HDA driver like vfio-pci is bound, the
drvdata is not a snd_card, and dereferencing it panics the kernel.

Add a check that the audio PCI device is actually bound to snd_hda_intel
before accessing its driver data.

Fixes: NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules#1365
Signed-off-by: bodapatisaikrishna <saikrishnabodapati@gmail.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
index df5a5e0e5..94223cb87 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
@@ -5952,6 +5952,16 @@ void NV_API_CALL nv_audio_dynamic_power(
     if (audio_pci_dev->dev.power.is_suspended)
         return;
 
+    /*
+     * Verify the audio function is bound to the HDA driver before accessing
+     * its driver data. When a different driver (e.g. vfio-pci) is bound,
+     * pci_get_drvdata() returns unrelated data and interpreting it as
+     * struct snd_card causes a kernel panic.
+     */
+    if (audio_pci_dev->driver == NULL ||
+        strcmp(audio_pci_dev->driver->name, "snd_hda_intel") != 0)
+        return;
+
     card = pci_get_drvdata(audio_pci_dev);
     if (card == NULL)
         return;
